  "comment": "MIXED TRIANGLE + HEXAGON BUBBLE TILES. Built for the two cells Chase, Field & McCluer leave as Unknown in Table 2: the (T,H) rows at ratio 2:3 with bite pairs (0,4) and (3,2), and at 4:3 with (0,5) and (3,1). All four satisfy the balance equation and none has a known realization. 18 tiles: the 4 binary necklaces of length 3 and the 14 of length 6, same complementary rule as bubble-tri / bubble-sq / bubble-hex. Angles in D=24 units: 60 = 4, 120 = 8, so the angle-valid vertices are 6x60, 3x120, 4x60+120 and 2x60+2x120 - valence 3 to 6, hence maxValence 6. NAMING at three hexagonal bites follows this repo (3A/3B/3C/3D) and not the paper (3A/3A*/3B/3C); same partition, different labels. The SEARCH needs EU_EDGE_COMPL=1 and the developer --complement.",
